<section class="bg-surface" aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20 sm:py-24">
    <h2
      id="problem-heading"
      class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-primary sm:text-4xl"
    >
      The tool got bought. The work never changed.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        You have the subscriptions. Someone ran a pilot. There was a training
        session, and a deck about adoption. And the team still keeps the old
        spreadsheet open on the second monitor, because nobody rebuilt the
        handoffs the tool was supposed to replace.
      </p>
      <p>
        That gap is rarely a technology problem. It is the last few inches
        between a capable system and the way work actually moves through your
        business — the re-typing, the waiting on an approval, the status meeting
        that exists only to find out where something is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
